We begin with the unfinished exercise from the preceding lecture. The horizontal and vertical polarization states are $\ket{x}=
  \begin{pmatrix}1\\0\end{pmatrix},
  \qquad
  \ket{y}=
  \begin{pmatrix}0\\1\end{pmatrix},$ and the observable that records $+1$ for horizontal transmission and $-1$ for vertical transmission is $\hat P_0=
  \begin{pmatrix}
    1&0\\
    0&-1
  \end{pmatrix}.$ At $45^\circ$, the two eigenstates $\ket{d_\pm}
  =\frac{1}{\sqrt2}
    \begin{pmatrix}1\\ \pm1\end{pmatrix}$ belong to $\hat P_{\pi/4}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    0&1\\
    1&0
  \end{pmatrix}.$

