p.src:
The homework was to construct the observable for the circular basis $\ket{c_+}
  =\frac{1}{\sqrt2}
    \begin{pmatrix}1\\i\end{pmatrix},
  \qquad
  \ket{c_-}
  =\frac{1}{\sqrt2}
    \begin{pmatrix}1\\-i\end{pmatrix}.$ The spectral rule gives the answer immediately: $\begin{aligned}
  \hat P_c
  &=
  \ket{c_+}\bra{c_+}
  -\ket{c_-}\bra{c_-}\\
  &=
  \begin{pmatrix}
    0&-i\\
    i&0
  \end{pmatrix}.
  \end{aligned}$ Indeed, $\hat P_c\ket{c_\pm}=\pm\ket{c_\pm}.$ The only delicate point in the check is $i^2=-1$, together with complex conjugation when a ket becomes a bra.

