The physical object is therefore not one normalized vector but the equivalence class $\ket{\psi}\sim e^{i\chi}\ket{\psi}.$ Such an equivalence class is called a ray in Hilbert space. In particular, $\begin{pmatrix}0\\1\end{pmatrix}
  \sim
  \begin{pmatrix}0\\-1\end{pmatrix},$ because $-1=e^{i\pi}$. Likewise, $\frac{1}{\sqrt2}
  \begin{pmatrix}1\\i\end{pmatrix}
  \sim
  \frac{1}{\sqrt2}
  \begin{pmatrix}i\\-1\end{pmatrix},$ because the second vector is $i$ times the first.

