Let $b=\sqrt{1-a^2},
  \qquad
  \ket{\psi}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}a\\be^{i\phi}\end{pmatrix},$ and compare it with a linearly polarized analyzer state $\ket{\theta}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \cos\theta\\
    \sin\theta
  \end{pmatrix}.$ The two conjugate amplitudes are $\begin{aligned}
  \braket{\theta}{\psi}
  &=a\cos\theta+be^{i\phi}\sin\theta,\\
  \braket{\psi}{\theta}
  &=a\cos\theta+be^{-i\phi}\sin\theta.
  \end{aligned}$

