Taking the adjoint of Equation  gives $\bra{A}\hat L^\dagger=\bra{C}.$ The defining matrix-element identity is $\boxed{
  \bra{B}\hat L\ket{A}
  =
  \left(
    \bra{A}\hat L^\dagger\ket{B}
  \right)^*.}$ It combines two operations already familiar from inner products: interchange bra and ket, then complex conjugate.

