p.src:
A unitary transformation is not the identity. It may rotate polarization, implement a symmetry, or carry a state from one time to another. Its adjoint undoes it, and throughout the motion $\braket{UB}{UA}
  =
  \bra{B}\hat U^\dagger\hat U\ket{A}
  =
  \braket{B}{A}.$ Thus every norm, orthogonality relation, and transition probability is preserved.

